{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 1319,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When I first heard about using particle accelerators\nto create solar panels, I thought… what?!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6099,
    "dDurationMs": 4341,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I must not understand how solar panels are\nmade. Or how particle accelerators work? And"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10440,
    "dDurationMs": 4139,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "yes, there’s a key, unglamorous step that\n– unless you’re fairly familiar with solar"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14579,
    "dDurationMs": 3831,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "manufacturing technology (which I’m not)\n– you probably wouldn’t think of, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 18410,
    "dDurationMs": 4109,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it’s in this step where a particle accelerator\nturns out to be useful: cutting silicon into"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22519,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the really thin wafers that are the key component\nof a solar panel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26259,
    "dDurationMs": 3651,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "However, even this wasn’t at all what I\nfirst thought, which was something like slicing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29910,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "through the crystal with a super powerful\nparticle beam. That sounds awesome, but the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 33770,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "actual technique is much less insane and much\nmore clever."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37030,
    "dDurationMs": 5380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ok, so a typical solar panel cell begins as\na carefully grown cylinder of silicon atoms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42410,
    "dDurationMs": 5660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "arranged in a regular crystal lattice, which\nare then trimmed and cut into wafer-thin…wafers."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 48070,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some of which retain curved corners as hallmarks\nof the original cylindrical crystal."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52700,
    "dDurationMs": 3900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then the wafers get covered with other metals,\nanti-reflective coatings and electrodes, and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 56600,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so on, to be able to capture the sun’s energy\n– but the part we want to focus on is the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 61220,
    "dDurationMs": 4269,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cutting. Because when you cut something with\na saw, like silicon wafers normally are, there"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 65489,
    "dDurationMs": 4981,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are two problems: one, you can't cut a slice\ntoo thin otherwise it might get broken – typical"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 70470,
    "dDurationMs": 6009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "solar panel wafers are cut to about 0.15 millimeters.\nAnd two, unlike a knife which cuts by separating"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76479,
    "dDurationMs": 5151,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and wedging two pieces of material apart,\na saw cuts with teeth that gouge and eat away"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81630,
    "dDurationMs": 5309,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the material, turning it into saw-dust\nand leaving a gap called a kerf. In the case"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 86939,
    "dDurationMs": 4691,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of silicon wafers, the gap is roughly the\nsame width as the wafers themselves, which"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91630,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "means about half of the original material\ngoes to waste!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94960,
    "dDurationMs": 4250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is where particle accelerators come in: not\nas a high powered ablative cutting particle"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 99210,
    "dDurationMs": 4939,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "beam, but by taking advantage of the physics\nof crystals. If instead you shoot protons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 104149,
    "dDurationMs": 4430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "with a certain energy at the flat face of\nthe silicon cylinder, those protons will embed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 108579,
    "dDurationMs": 4551,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "themselves into the silicon. The depth depends\non how much energy they have, and the thinner"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113130,
    "dDurationMs": 4291,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you want, the less energy they take, so you\ncan easily pick something super thin. But"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117421,
    "dDurationMs": 4268,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whatever thickness you choose, once inside\nthe silicon crystal lattice, the protons kind"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 121689,
    "dDurationMs": 4110,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of push it apart and create stress; if you\nheat the whole thing up, a wafer will break"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 125799,
    "dDurationMs": 5001,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "right off, cleanly cleaving along the crystal\nlattice lines where the protons were. So,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130800,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if after the protons are embedded, but before\nthe heating, you glue this proto-wafer onto"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135720,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a piece of glass or plastic, and then heat\nit up, you end up with a nice thin wafer of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139950,
    "dDurationMs": 5130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "silicon attached to a durable (and possibly\nflexible) material, with no waste silicon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145080,
    "dDurationMs": 3010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whatsoever. To me, this is clever physics\nengineering!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148090,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of course, a particle accelerator is much\nmore expensive than a saw, so there must be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152490,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some upsides to it – the biggest is that,\nby using significantly less silicon per wafer"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157400,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and not losing any silicon in the cutting\nprocess, it’s possible to justify using"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161060,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much more expensive silicon that’s better\nat capturing sunlight, meaning the resultant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164920,
    "dDurationMs": 4490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "solar panels for a given power output are\nsmaller and need less other material to make"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169410,
    "dDurationMs": 4290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "them and hold them up, hence they’re cheaper.\nHopefully enough cheaper to make up for the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 173700,
    "dDurationMs": 4550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "extra costs of using a particle accelerator\nto part silicon!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178250,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The company that’s trying to use the particle-accelerator\ntechnology I talked about in this video to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 182240,
    "dDurationMs": 4700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "make solar cells on a commercial scale, this\ncompany is called Rayton Solar. This is a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 186940,
    "dDurationMs": 3830,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "challenging and expensive endeavor and they’re\nlooking for investors, so they sponsored this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 190770,
    "dDurationMs": 6850,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "video to get the word out - startengine.com/startup/rayton-solar.\nI’m not going to make any endorsement – I"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 197620,
    "dDurationMs": 3980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "mean, I’m neither an investment expert,\nnor a solar industry expert – but I do believe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 201600,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "strongly that we need both political and technological\nsolutions to secure our planet’s energy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 206190,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "future, so I’m happy to help Rayton reach\na broader audience to help give them a chance"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 209700,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for this clever idea to succeed, and I’m\nmaking a small investment myself. Hopefully"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213760,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they’ll end up being one of the many many\npieces that come together to provide a civilized"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 217280,
    "dDurationMs": 2510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "long-term future for humanity on earth."
    } ]
  } ]
}
